<title>USA: KingWorld beats Q3 estimates by a penny.</title>
<headline>KingWorld beats Q3 estimates by a penny.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>King World Productions Inc's third quarter earnings of $0.95 per share beat analysts' estimates for the quarter by the narrowest of margins.</p>
<p>A First Call consensus estimate of 10 brokers had put earnings at $0.94 per share.</p>
<p>The distributer of television programs such as Wheel of Fortune and the Oprah Winfrey show said it bought back 971,000 shares for a total of $36.2 million, or about $37.20 per share, through June 23.</p>
